Z||000000||turbo86se||07-16-2001||03:03 PM||||<BR>Hi Everyone!<BR>I just noticed while cleaning my '88 coupe, the passenger door doesn't have inner or outer dew wipes. Could this be the cause of a little water entering the interior under the door? <BR>The passenger door came from a '85 coupe at a boneyard (my coupe was wrecked when I bought it), the door hinges were real bad. I guess I should have picked a better door! My coupe and I have come a long way, she now has a V6!||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||07-16-2001||04:34 PM||||yep those dew wipes help kee the water out from inside your doors.you will need a special tool to get the outside ones off.some of us here were going keep passing this tool on to each other just for the postage this has been about a month since I've heard anything about it I was waiting in line also to get this tool. but I dont know who has it now but I beleive Rodney Dickmen sells this tool on his web site for not really sure but I think $15.00||||reg||1
Z||000002||jake1852||07-16-2001||04:47 PM||||hey turbo86se: what did you have to do to put a v6 in? i am considering it myself, and so far all ive learned is that i will need motor mounts,  engine, wiring harness, and computer. <BR>is there anything else that you had to do?<P>------------------<BR>- Unfinished ferrari kit, custom made myself<BR>-87 duke (just got it, its fast, and i dont know why yet!)<BR>- 87 GT<BR>- Tc Maserati (daily drive)||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||07-16-2001||11:33 PM||||hey jake,<BR>the installation was pretty straigtforward. I used a V6 from a '88 Formula in my '88 coupe. My mechanic installed a 3800 in a customer's Formula, so I bought the 2.8 from him. It had 55K miles on it, one owner, computer, wiring harness, in excellent shape, I won't say how much I paid for it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Finding a motor mount took time, had to find someone parting out a Formula. Luckily, searching ebay I found someone with the mount.<P>All the wiring snapped into place, but I lost count of all the trips to Advance for vaccumm lines, fuel hoses, radiator hose, heating/cooling lines, clamps, bolts, etc.<P>I bought a V6 starter off ebay, though I believe the original one from the 4 would work, I decided against it. <P>Fuel pump had to be replaced with a fuel pump from a V6 Fiero. Got that from Advance. <P>Stuck with stock radiator. Since I put in a new O2 sensor it hasn't come anywhere near overheating. <P>Needed auto detent/kickdown cable, and got a throttle cable from Fiero Store. <P>Guages had to be replaced with ones from a V6. I got a complete setup from Chris Pond on the Forum from an '88 GT. I put those guages into my '86SE and the SE guages into my coupe. Odometers swapped easily so it's all correct. Chris Pond (Pondski) is an excellent guy and I highly recommend him to anyone. I wouldn't hesitate to buy anything from Chris.<P>I also put in a new alternator, and got a V6 air cleaner housing from FieroDave, also from the Forum.<P>The passenger side drive shaft had to be replaced due to sitting for eight months in the air.<P>It needs shocks and struts next. It bounces easily, but still handles like it's on rails. I can't imagine it with KYB's.<P>I've had the V6 in it two months now, and put over 3500 miles on it, including a 1400 mile trip to Carlisle, PA for the show in May, four days after it was completed. No problems.<P>If you're ever in Myrtle Beach, SC, LMK I'll take you for a test drive!   ||||reg||1
